  "result": "Perfect! The payment terms implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Updated: `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID` error code\n\n**Updated: `src/invoices.js`**\n- Added `calculateDueDate()` helper function that:\n  - NET14: adds 14 days to issue date\n  - NET30: adds 30 days to issue date (default)\n  - EOM: calculates last day of the month using next month's first day minus 1\n  - Returns null for invalid terms\n- Modified `createInvoice()` to:\n  - Accept optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n  - Validate terms against allowed values\n  - Calculate and set `invoice.dueDate`\n  - Store `invoice.terms`\n  - Return `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown terms\n\n**Updated: `test/invoices.test.js`**\n- Added 11 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Default NET30 terms and correct due date calculation\n  - NET14 and EOM terms with correct due dates\n  - EOM edge cases: February (leap year), year boundary\n  - Invalid/empty terms validation\n  - Immutability of input\n\nAll 169 tests pass (158 existing + 11 new). Terms are properly validated, due dates calculated correctly for all scenarios, and invoices now include both `terms` and `dueDate` fields.",
